# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The above histogram shows the measurement results of all four qubits at the "
"end of the circuit. An ideal quantum computer with zero noise would have "
"measured the qubits to have the same values every time, but in reality, "
"noise will cause some of the runs to produce errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Histogram di atas menunjukkan hasil pengukuran dari keempat qubit di akhir "
"Circuit. Komputer kuantum ideal dengan nol noise akan selalu mengukur qubit "
"memiliki nilai yang sama setiap kali, tapi pada kenyataannya, noise akan "
"menyebabkan beberapa run menghasilkan kesalahan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-8}"
msgstr "Cek pemahamanmu {#check-your-understanding-8}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the bitstring with the most counts as your values for $A$, $B$, $S$, "
"and $C$, verify that the quantum adder circuit worked.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan bitstring dengan jumlah terbanyak sebagai nilai kamu untuk $A$, "
"$B$, $S$, dan $C$, verifikasi bahwa Circuit quantum adder bekerja.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We need to verify that $A+B = S+2 \\times C$. Remember that the bitstring "
"order follows little-endian notation, so it is read `CSBA`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita perlu memverifikasi bahwa $A+B = S+2 \\times C$. Ingat bahwa urutan "
"bitstring mengikuti notasi little-endian, jadi dibaca `CSBA`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the histogram above, we see that the `0000` bitstring is the dominant "
"one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dari histogram di atas, kita melihat bahwa bitstring `0000` adalah yang "
"dominan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$0 + 0 = 0 + 0 \\times 2 = 0 ~\\checkmark$$\n"
msgstr "$$0 + 0 = 0 + 0 \\times 2 = 0 ~\\checkmark$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Go back and change the values of $A$ and $B$ to $A=1$ and $B=1$ and go "
"through the Qiskit patterns steps again to rerun the circuit. Verify that "
"the adder circuit worked again.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kembali dan ubah nilai $A$ dan $B$ menjadi $A=1$ dan $B=1$ lalu jalani "
"kembali langkah-langkah Qiskit patterns untuk menjalankan ulang Circuit. "
"Verifikasi bahwa Circuit adder bekerja lagi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should obtain a histogram with the dominant bitstring being `1011`:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu seharusnya mendapatkan histogram dengan bitstring dominan `1011`:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$1 + 1 = 0 + 1 \\times 2 = 2 ~\\checkmark$$\n"
msgstr "$$1 + 1 = 0 + 1 \\times 2 = 2 ~\\checkmark$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One of the added features of the *quantum* half-adder over the classical "
"half-adder is that it can run with *quantum* inputs. That is, it can \"add\""
" qubits $A$ and $B$ even if they are in superposition states. In the "
"Challenge Questions section below, you will be asked to prepare the qubits "
"in superpositions and see what happens!\n"
msgstr ""
"Salah satu fitur tambahan dari quantum half-adder dibanding classical half-"
"adder adalah bahwa ia bisa berjalan dengan input *kuantum*. Artinya, ia bisa"
" \"menjumlahkan\" Qubit $A$ dan $B$ meskipun keduanya berada dalam keadaan "
"superposisi. Di bagian Pertanyaan Tantangan di bawah, kamu akan diminta "
"untuk mempersiapkan qubit dalam superposisi dan melihat apa yang terjadi!\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr "Kesimpulan {#conclusion}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This module was designed to give you a firm foundational understanding of "
"the basic principles behind quantum computing by comparing it to classical "
"computing. We looked at the classical half-adder circuit and then showed you"
" how to adapt the circuit to run with qubits on a quantum computer. Now "
"you're ready to explore the other Qiskit in the Classroom modules!\n"
msgstr ""
"Modul ini dirancang untuk memberimu pemahaman dasar yang kuat tentang "
"prinsip-prinsip dasar di balik komputasi kuantum dengan membandingkannya "
"dengan komputasi klasik. Kita melihat Circuit classical half-adder lalu "
"menunjukkan cara mengadaptasi Circuit tersebut untuk dijalankan dengan qubit"
" di komputer kuantum. Sekarang kamu siap untuk menjelajahi modul-modul "
"Qiskit in the Classroom lainnya!\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts: {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Konsep penting: {#critical-concepts}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In contrast to classical bits which can only take on values 0 and 1, qubits "
"can also be in **superposition** states of both 0 and 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berbeda dengan bit klasik yang hanya bisa mengambil nilai 0 dan 1, qubit "
"juga bisa berada dalam keadaan **superposisi** dari keduanya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Multiple qubits can be in a superposition over the classically allowed "
"bitstrings called **computational basis states**.\n"
msgstr ""
"Beberapa qubit bisa berada dalam superposisi atas bitstring yang diizinkan "
"secara klasik yang disebut **keadaan basis komputasi**.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Multiple qubits can be **entangled** so that the state of one depends on the"
" state of the other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Beberapa qubit bisa **terjerat** sehingga keadaan satu bergantung pada "
"keadaan yang lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit convention is to use **little-endian notation**, which places the"
" least significant qubit, $q_0$, in the rightmost position and the most "
"significant qubit, $q_N$, leftmost.\n"
msgstr ""
"Konvensi Qiskit adalah menggunakan **notasi little-endian**, yang "
"menempatkan qubit paling tidak signifikan, $q_0$, di posisi paling kanan dan"
" qubit paling signifikan, $q_N$, paling kiri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quantum gates** are reversible operations that are represented by unitary "
"matrices which act on the quantum state vectors. In this notation, the "
"matrix closest to the vector (which is furthest right) acts first.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gate kuantum** adalah operasi reversibel yang direpresentasikan oleh "
"matriks uniter yang bekerja pada vektor keadaan kuantum. Dalam notasi ini, "
"matriks yang paling dekat dengan vektor (yang paling kanan) bertindak "
"pertama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Measurements** collapse a quantum superposition state into one of its "
"classically allowed states, with probability equal to the square of the "
"amplitude of the corresponding computational basis state in the "
"superposition.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pengukuran** meruntuhkan keadaan superposisi kuantum menjadi salah satu "
"keadaan yang diizinkan secara klasik, dengan probabilitas sama dengan "
"kuadrat amplitudo keadaan basis komputasi yang sesuai dalam superposisi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits are often represented using **quantum circuit diagrams**, "
"where qubits are depicted as horizontal wires, and quantum gates appear "
"along these wires from left to right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Circuit kuantum sering direpresentasikan menggunakan **diagram Circuit "
"kuantum**, di mana qubit digambarkan sebagai kabel horizontal, dan Gate "
"kuantum muncul di sepanjang kabel ini dari kiri ke kanan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To run a quantum circuit, we use the four steps in the **Qiskit patterns** "
"workflow: **Map**, **Optimize**, **Execute**, **Post-process**.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menjalankan Circuit kuantum, kita menggunakan empat langkah dalam alur"
" kerja **Qiskit patterns**: **Peta**, **Optimasi**, **Eksekusi**, **Pasca-"
"proses**.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Questions {#questions}"
msgstr "Pertanyaan {#questions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "True/False Questions {#truefalse-questions}"
msgstr "Pertanyaan Benar/Salah {#truefalse-questions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A single bit in a classical computer can only hold the value 0 or 1.\n"
msgstr "Satu bit dalam komputer klasik hanya bisa menyimpan nilai 0 atau 1.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Entanglement means the state of one qubit is independent of the state of "
"another.\n"
msgstr ""
"Keterikatan berarti keadaan satu qubit tidak bergantung pada keadaan qubit "
"lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum gates are generally irreversible operations.\n"
msgstr "Gate kuantum umumnya adalah operasi yang tidak reversibel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit convention places the least significant qubit, $q_0$, at the "
"leftmost position.\n"
msgstr ""
"Konvensi Qiskit menempatkan qubit paling tidak signifikan, $q_0$, di posisi "
"paling kiri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measuring a quantum state always gives the exact same result if repeated "
"many times.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengukur keadaan kuantum selalu memberikan hasil yang sama persis jika "
"diulang berkali-kali.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Hadamard gate creates superposition in a single qubit.\n"
msgstr "Gate Hadamard menciptakan superposisi dalam satu qubit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits may include measurement operations that collapse the "
"superposition state into one of the classically allowed states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Circuit kuantum mungkin menyertakan operasi pengukuran yang meruntuhkan "
"keadaan superposisi menjadi salah satu keadaan yang diizinkan secara "
"klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '8. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The number of possible classical states for $N$ bits is $2N$.\n"
msgstr "Jumlah kemungkinan keadaan klasik untuk $N$ bit adalah $2N$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '9. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The outcome probabilities for quantum measurements are given by the squared "
"amplitudes of the classically measurable basis states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Probabilitas hasil untuk pengukuran kuantum diberikan oleh kuadrat amplitudo"
" keadaan basis yang dapat diukur secara klasik.\n"

